{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 201, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "Raising a very small learning rate fixes underfitting within 243 epochs (exps 1, 2, 17), giving large gains compared with elsewhere."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "At already-large learning rates, a further increase makes Adam training diverge (exps 5, 9, 19, 20)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Lowering an unstable, too-large learning rate recovers trainability, a much larger benefit than lowering a moderate one."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Increasing an already-strong L2 penalty causes heavy underfitting (exps 45, 57-60), while small alphas are harmless to raise (41-43)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "batch_size", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "With tiny batches the L2 penalty is applied far more often per epoch, so raising alpha hurts much more (exps 52, 54 vs 53, 55)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper nets are less stable at large learning rates, so adding a layer there collapses accuracy (exps 84, 85, 94)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At small learning rates the extra layer adds capacity and speeds fitting without instability (exps 83, 86, 93)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "batch_size", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "Small batche